st_budget.py` is scaffold the plan forbids editing. That makes this a plan-level gap, but it is still a regression hole in shipped code.\n\n**Fix:** Add a new test file, for example `tests/test_budget_window.py`. Put named constants `FAILOVER_SECS = 90` and `PAGER_ESCALATION_SECS = 240` in `probe/budget.py` and use them in the comment. Assert `FAILOVER_SECS < DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS < PAGER_ESCALATION_SECS`.\n\n### WR-02: Conflicting base-branch configuration (`devflow.toml` vs `.planning/config.json`)\n\n**File:** `devflow.toml:1` and `.planning/config.json` (`git.base_branch`)\n**Issue:**\n- `devflow.toml` sets `base_branch = \"integration\"`.\n- `.planning/config.json` sets `\"base_branch\": \"main\"`.\n- `feature/phase-01` descends from `integration`, which is 1 commit ahead of `main` (it holds only the devflow.toml commit).\n- Which key a PR or merge tool honours depends on the consumer, and neither consumer is in the repo. A GSD `ship` or PR step could target `main` and carry the config commit along, or skip `integration`.\n- Nothing in the artifacts records which is authoritative.\n\n**Fix:** Decide the intended merge target and make the two files agree. Set `.planning/config.json` `git.base_branch` to `\"integration\"`, or remove the `devflow.toml` override. At minimum, confirm the target explicitly before merging.\n\n### WR-03: VERIFICATION.md carries a timestamp from the future (false attestation)\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERIFICATION.md:3` (`verified: 2026-10-07T22:40:00Z`)\n**Issue:**\n- The file was committed in b8f17b0 at 2026-10-07T18:27:34-04:00, which is 22:27:34Z. `STATE.md` `last_updated` is 22:27:34Z.\n- My own `date -u` at review time was 22:30:44Z.\n- A `verified:` time of 22:40:00Z is therefore about 12 minutes after the commit that contains it, and in the future when I checked.\n- It looks hand-written or rounded rather than measured. Downstream tooling that orders artifacts by `verified:` against commit or review t